WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.230
- In addition to

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.710
Black Lives Matter,

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:05.490
there's also a movement for
Black trans lives matter.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.409
- Yes.

00:00:06.409 --> 00:00:07.380
- Could you talk a little about that?

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.470
- Yeah, you know,

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:09.583
I got a lot of heat.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.950
I did a message to America on my

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.223
Instagram,

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.923
and I got a lotta heat for
calling Black people out.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.450
The relationship that the
African-American community has

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.960
with the LGBTQ+ community,

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.490
it is

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.760
not good,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.290
and trans women,

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.920
specifically Black trans women,

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.330
trans women of color,

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.340
are dying at the hands of cis Black men

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.488
at alarming rates.

00:00:46.488 --> 00:00:47.321
- Wow.

00:00:47.321 --> 00:00:48.571
- And what I'm saying is,

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:53.600
it's a simple do unto others metaphor,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.509
right.

00:00:54.509 --> 00:00:55.342
- Mhm.

00:00:55.342 --> 00:00:58.450
- We want somebody to stop killin' us,

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:02.207
we have to make sure that
we have our house in order.

00:01:02.207 --> 00:01:03.040
- Mhm.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:03.873
- Period.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.760
And it's a conversation

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.640
that pose presents,

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.580
it's an uncomfortable conversation.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.770
You know, because

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.040
trans lives

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.890
are the next on the list

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:24.270
of dismissible humans.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.620
Trans people are human beings,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.820
I'm a gay man,

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.560
but I'm a Black man first,

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.363
and until Black people understand that,

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.210
we're gonna be in the quagmire

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:39.030
goin' round and round.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.990
You can't expect

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:43.520
somebody else to change,

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.570
until we can look at ourselves,

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.700
and make that transformation
within ourselves.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.640
- I mean I think that's,

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.100
that's applicable to

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:51.933
all of us.

00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:52.766
- Yes.

00:01:52.766 --> 00:01:54.750
- You know, even in whatever
your situation is in life,

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.790
and whatever you're going through in your

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:57.300
personal hurdles, and challenges,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.560
like I think you know,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.880
you can't expect others to do that

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.498
unless you're willing to do it yourself.

00:02:01.498 --> 00:02:02.331
- Correct.

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:04.360
- And really take a look in that mirror,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.193
so I think,

00:02:05.193 --> 00:02:06.680
I think that it's amazing

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.953
that you're standing up for everyone.

